// `relax.k`: jumps on either side of the short form's reach. Each function skips a body of n
// statements with an `if` and loops over one of n/2, for n from 4 to 24, so somewhere along the
// way a forward and a backward jump pass 128 bytes. NASM refuses a short jump that does not reach,
// so assembling at all checks the bounds; running checks every jump went where it should. The
// expected values were computed outside the compiler at the same 64-bit wrap.

